---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Best Time to Visit Dujiangyan Panda Base - Season Guide"
  description="Season-by-season guide to visiting Dujiangyan Panda Base: weather, crowds, panda activity, and what to expect each month of the year."
>
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-accent-600 uppercase mb-3">Best Time</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-warm-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">
      Best Time to Visit Dujiangyan Panda Base
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-warm-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
      Spring and autumn offer the best weather and most active pandas. Here is what each season and month looks like.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-warm-500">Last updated: July 2026</p>
  </section>

  <!-- Season Overview -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-12">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-5">Season Overview</h2>
    <div class="space-y-5">
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border bg-green-50 border-green-200">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-warm-900 text-lg">Spring</h3>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-green-200 text-green-800">Best</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Mar - May (15-25 C)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Mild temperatures, bamboo is lush and green, pandas are active outdoors. March can still be cool with occasional rain. April and May are ideal — comfortable weather and active pandas before the summer heat arrives. This is the best window to visit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-200">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-warm-900 text-lg">Summer</h3>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-yellow-200 text-yellow-800">Good</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Jun - Aug (25-35 C)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Hot and humid with frequent afternoon thunderstorms. Pandas retreat to shaded areas and air-conditioned indoor spaces by midday. Morning visits (arrive at 8:30 AM) are essential — pandas are most active during the cooler morning hours. July and August are also peak domestic travel season (Chinese school holidays), so expect larger crowds despite the heat.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border bg-orange-50 border-orange-200">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-warm-900 text-lg">Autumn</h3>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-orange-200 text-orange-800">Best</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Sep - Nov (15-25 C)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Crisp, clear days with beautiful fall colors. Pandas are active and playful. September and October are excellent — similar conditions to spring but with even clearer skies. November cools down but remains pleasant. Avoid the first week of October (Golden Week national holiday) when the entire country travels and the base gets very crowded.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border bg-blue-50 border-blue-200">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-2">
          <h3 class="font-semibold text-warm-900 text-lg">Winter</h3>
          <span class="text-xs font-medium px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-200 text-blue-800">Okay</span>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-warm-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Dec - Feb (0-10 C)</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">Cold but much quieter. Pandas remain active — they have thick fur and actually enjoy the cooler temperatures. The base is nearly empty of tourists, giving you a peaceful experience. Some paths may be icy. Dress in warm layers. Chinese New Year (usually January/February) brings a brief spike in visitors but also festive decorations at the base.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Month by Month -->
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 pb-24 md:pb-32">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mb-5">Month by Month</h2>
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-warm-200 bg-white">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-warm-100">
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Month</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Temp (C)</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Crowds</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Panda Activity</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-medium text-warm-700">Rating</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-warm-200">
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Jan</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">3-9</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very low</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Feb</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">5-12</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Low (except CNY)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Mar</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">10-17</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Moderate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Active</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Apr</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">15-23</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Moderate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very active</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">May</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">19-27</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Busy</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Active (mornings)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Jun</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">22-30</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Moderate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Lazy (hot)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Jul</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">24-33</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very busy</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Lazy (hot)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Okay</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Aug</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">23-32</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very busy</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Lazy (hot)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Okay</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Sep</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">19-27</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Moderate</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very active</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Oct</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">15-22</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Busy (Golden Week)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very active</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Nov</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">10-16</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Low</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Active</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-accent-700 font-medium">Excellent</td></tr>
          <tr class="bg-warm-50"><td class="px-4 py-2.5 font-medium text-warm-900">Dec</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">4-10</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Very low</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-warm-600">Good</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
      Weather data reflects typical conditions for the Dujiangyan area at approximately 700m elevation. Always check the forecast before your visit — Sichuan weather can be unpredictable, especially in summer.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-warm-600 leading-relaxed">
      If you are also visiting the nearby UNESCO sites, check our <a href="/nearby-attractions" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">nearby attractions guide</a> for tips on combining your panda visit with the Dujiangyan Irrigation System and Mount Qingcheng.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
